monero_c: link desktop Linux with a static C++ runtime and export only the C API.

The linux-gnu library linked libstdc++ and libgcc_s dynamically, so it needed
the runtime of the GCC that built it. With simplybs' GCC 15 toolchain that is
GLIBCXX_3.4.32 and CXXABI_1.3.15, which no distribution older than about 2023
ships, whatever its glibc:

    NEEDED  libstdc++.so.6 libm.so.6 libgcc_s.so.1 libc.so.6 ld-linux-x86-64.so.2

Link it statically, exactly as the mingw targets a few lines up already do.
Only libc, libm and the loader remain, and the GCC version stops mattering to
anyone loading the library. (The glibc half of the same problem is the
toolchain's, not this file's; see 0014.)

A static runtime makes the export list matter. libstdc++'s headers force
default visibility on namespace std, so template instantiations compiled into
this library are exported despite -fvisibility=hidden. The Sep 17 build
exported three:

    std::vector<std::string>::_M_realloc_append<std::string>
    std::vector<std::string>::_M_realloc_append<std::string const&>
    std::vector<unsigned long>::_M_realloc_append<unsigned long>

Harmless while the runtime was shared. With a private copy inside, a process
that also loads the system libstdc++ -- the desktop wallet does, through
WebKitGTK -- could have the two runtimes binding each other's symbols. The
existing --exclude-libs,ALL hides archive members but not these, which come
from our own objects. A version script keeping <FLAVOR>_* global and
everything else local does. It is generated rather than committed so the same
file serves monero, wownero and zano, and it deliberately keeps data symbols:
the enum constants (MONERO_NetworkType_MAINNET and friends) are OBJECTs and
part of the API.

-z relro -z now: monero's CMakeLists puts its hardening linker flags in
CMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS only, so the shared library got partial RELRO with a
GOT left writable after startup. -z noexecstack is restated because the
LINK_FLAGS set_target_properties further down replaces the one set for
linux-gnu above it; target_link_options is used here so these cannot be
lost the same way.

Not added: -fcf-protection / -mbranch-protection. monero already compiles its
own code with -fcf-protection=full, but the linker only marks the output IBT/
SHSTK when every input object is, and the static libstdc++ and the simplybs
dependencies are not built that way, so the flag here would change nothing.

Verified on x86_64-linux-gnu against the cached Sep 17 toolchain: links
cleanly (the static libstdc++ in the crosstool-NG toolchain is PIC enough for
a shared object), NEEDED is libm, libc and ld-linux only, FLAGS_1 has NOW, 358
exports all MONERO_*, and the xmr and cxmr Go tests pass against it.

--- a/monero_libwallet2_api_c/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/monero_libwallet2_api_c/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -71,6 +71,36 @@ if(${HOST_ABI} STREQUAL "x86_64-w64-mingw32" OR ${HOST_ABI} STREQUAL "i686-w64-m
     target_link_options(${MONERO_FLAVOR}_wallet2_api_c PRIVATE -static-libgcc -static-libstdc++)
 endif()
 
+# Desktop Linux: depend on nothing newer than the toolchain's glibc.
+#
+# With the C++ runtime linked dynamically the library needs the libstdc++ of
+# the GCC that built it (GLIBCXX_3.4.32 for GCC 13+), which no distribution
+# older than about 2023 ships. Link it statically, as mingw already does above,
+# so only libc, libm and the loader remain.
+#
+# The version script then keeps the C API and nothing else. libstdc++ headers
+# force default visibility on the std namespace, so template instantiations
+# compiled into this library are exported despite -fvisibility=hidden, and with
+# a static runtime inside, a host process that also loads the system libstdc++
+# (the desktop wallet does, through WebKitGTK) could bind across the two.
+# --exclude-libs,ALL below hides the archive members but not those.
+#
+# -z relro -z now: monero's own hardening flags go to CMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS
+# only, so this shared library got partial RELRO with a writable GOT.
+#
+# target_link_options, not LINK_FLAGS: the set_target_properties below replaces
+# LINK_FLAGS wholesale, which is how the -z noexecstack above is already lost.
+if(${HOST_ABI} MATCHES "-linux-gnu")
+    string(TOUPPER "${MONERO_FLAVOR}" FLAVOR_PREFIX)
+    set(VERSION_SCRIPT "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/${MONERO_FLAVOR}_wallet2_api_c.map")
+    file(WRITE "${VERSION_SCRIPT}" "{ global: ${FLAVOR_PREFIX}_*; local: *; };\n")
+    target_link_options(${MONERO_FLAVOR}_wallet2_api_c PRIVATE
+        -static-libgcc -static-libstdc++
+        "-Wl,--version-script,${VERSION_SCRIPT}"
+        -Wl,-z,relro -Wl,-z,now -Wl,-z,noexecstack)
+    set_property(TARGET ${MONERO_FLAVOR}_wallet2_api_c APPEND PROPERTY LINK_DEPENDS "${VERSION_SCRIPT}")
+endif()
+
 if (${MONERO_FLAVOR} STREQUAL "monero")
     target_compile_definitions(${MONERO_FLAVOR}_wallet2_api_c PRIVATE FLAVOR_MONERO)
     set(BCUR_ENABLED bc-ur)
